{
  "rationale": "The plant automata model the robot's perception (sensors) and actuation (motion commands) as separate, event-driven systems. The specification automata bind perception outcomes to safe, coverage-oriented actions, enforcing conservative recovery only when obstacles are detected and returning to exploration as soon as the path is clear. The design ensures every state has a controllable action, obstacle events force recovery, and exploration is prioritized when safe.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for perception and motion, with all events as specified.",
    "Specification automata encode safe, progress-oriented policies: forward/random_walk in clear, rotate or back out on obstacle, and quick return to exploration after recovery."
  ],
